  "subject": "Exact emission rejection rules and canonical nominal names",
  "claim": "The emitter propagates the rejection rule from the failing analysis branch and resolves nominal names through canonical symbol order. A maintained source fixture deliberately separates declaration order from canonical order and reproduces ownership-analysis exhaustion. Seven cases pass on each native host for both the maintained fixture and the original Package-Lock snapshots. Successful WVB bytes, malformed-input exits and pre-existing output preservation remain unchanged.",
